hadiths[123]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1189","[AI-translation] Darda', who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, came out to us while we were mentioning poverty and fearing it. He said: ""Is it poverty that you fear?! By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the world will surely be poured upon you pouring until the heart of none of you deviates except towards it. By Allah, I have left you upon the like of the white (path), its night and day being the same."" Abu Ad-Darda' said: ""The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, spoke the truth—by Allah. He left us, by Allah, upon the like of the white, its night and day being the same."
"1190","[AI-translation] From 'Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said to Umm Hani': ""Keep sheep, for indeed in them is blessing."
"1191","[AI-translation] 'As: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, sent 'Itab bin Usaid to Makkah, and said: ""Do you know to where I am sending you? To the people of Allah, and they are the people of Makkah. So forbid them four things: a sale and a loan, two conditions in a sale, profit on what one does not guarantee, and selling what is not with you."
"1192","[AI-translation] From Mahmud bin Labid, raised to the Prophet: ""There are two things that the son of Adam dislikes: he dislikes death, while death is better for the believer than tribulation; and he dislikes having little wealth, while having little wealth is lighter for the reckoning."
"1193","On the authority of a man from the Ansar, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the funeral of a man from the Ansar. When we returned, we encountered the messenger of a woman from Quraysh, who said: ""So-and-so invites you and those with you to a meal."" So he turned back, sat down, and we sat with him. The food was brought. The Prophet ﷺ placed his hand [to eat], and the people placed their hands. They watched the Prophet ﷺ, and when a morsel was in his mouth he could not swallow it. So they restrained their hands to see what the Prophet ﷺ would do. He took his morsel and spat it out, saying: ""I find the meat of a sheep taken without the permission of its owners. Feed it to the captives."""
"1194","[AI-translation] Sa'idi, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Be moderate in seeking this worldly life, for everyone is facilitated for what he was created."
"1195","[AI-translation] From 'Uqbah bin 'Amir, who said: A man came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and said: My mother passed away and left jewelry and did not make a will; will it benefit her if I give charity on her behalf? He said: Keep your wealth to yourself."
"1196","[AI-translation] From Mus'ab bin Sa'd, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Beware of this world, for it is green and sweet."
"1197","[AI-translation] From Ziyad bin Husayn, from his father Husayn bin Qays: That he carried food to al-Madinah and met the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, who said: What are you carrying, O Bedouin? He said: Wheat. He said: What did you intend with it, or what do you intend with it?! He said: I intended to sell it. So he wiped my head and said: Treat the Bedouin well in transactions."
"1198","[AI-translation] From Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: My maternal aunt was divorced three times, so she went out to pollinate her palm trees. A man met her and forbade her, so she came to the Prophet, peace be upon him, and mentioned that to him. He said to her: Go out and pollinate your palm trees, perhaps you may give charity from it or do good."
"1199","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu'an: Render the trust to the one who entrusted you, and do not betray the one who betrayed you."
"1200","[AI-translation] From 'Uthman bin 'Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, admitted a man into Paradise who was easygoing when buying, selling, judging, and seeking fulfillment."
"1201","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud, marfu'an: If the two parties to a sale disagree and there is no proof between them, then it is what the owner of the goods says, or they cancel the transaction."
"1202","[AI-translation] From Muhammad bin Yahya bin Habban who said: He is my grandfather Munqidh bin 'Amr, and he was a man who had been afflicted in his head, which impaired his speech. He would not abandon trade because of that, and he was constantly being cheated. He came to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and mentioned that to him. He said to him: When you trade, say: ""No deception,"" and then you have the option of three nights in every item you buy. If you are satisfied, keep it, and if you are dissatisfied, return it to its owner."
"1203","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: If any of you sells a sheep or a milch animal, he should not leave its milk undrawn."
"1204","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar, raised to the Prophet: When you engage in 'inah sales, hold the tails of cattle, become content with agriculture, and abandon jihad, Allah will impose upon you a humiliation which He will not remove until you return to your religion."
"1205","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas: That he (peace be upon him and his family) forbade the price of wine, the wage of a prostitute, and the price of a dog, and said: If someone comes to you demanding the price of a dog, fill his hands with dirt."
"1206","[AI-translation] Ansari informed him: that he was a governor over Al-Yamamah, and that Marwan wrote to him that Mu'awiyah had written to him that: Whichever man has something stolen from him, he has more right to it wherever he finds it. Then Marwan wrote that to me, and I wrote to Marwan that the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) judged that if the one who buys it—meaning the stolen item—from the one who stole it is not a suspect, its owner is given the choice: if he wishes, he takes what was stolen from him for its price, and if he wishes, he pursues its thief. Then Abu Bakr, 'Umar, and 'Uthman judged by that. So Marwan sent my letter to Mu'awiyah, and Mu'awiyah wrote to Marwan: You and Usaid do not pass judgment over me, rather I pass judgment in what I have appointed over you two, so execute what I have commanded you. Marwan sent Mu'awiyah's letter, and I said: I will not judge by it in what I have been appointed based on what Mu'awiyah said."
"1207","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: Four are hated by Allah, the Mighty and Sublime: the swearing seller, the arrogant poor man, the old man who commits adultery, and the unjust leader."
"1208","[AI-translation] Sa'idi who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) and said: O Messenger of Allah! Direct me to a deed which, if I do it, Allah will love me and people will love me. So the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Be indifferent to the world and Allah will love you, and be indifferent to what people have and people will love you."
"1209","[AI-translation] From Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) and said: I love you. He said: Prepare for poverty."
"1210","[AI-translation] Khudri from his father: that he complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) about his need, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Be patient, Abu Sa'id, for poverty comes to whoever among you loves me faster than a flood coming to the top of the valley and from the top of the mountain to its bottom."
"1211","[AI-translation] From Rafi' ibn Khadij who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) was asked: What is the purest earning? He said: The purest earning is a man's work by his hand, and every righteous sale."
"1212","[AI-translation] From Haram ibn Sa'd ibn Muhayyisah: That Muhayyisah asked the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) about the earnings of his cupper, so he forbade him from it, but he kept speaking to him until he said: Feed it to your pack-camel and feed your servants with it."
"1213","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: O Allah, make the provision of the family of Muhammad sufficient sustenance."
"1214","[AI-translation] From Ibn Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: Allah, Exalted is He, made the entirety of the world insignificant, and what remains of it is but a little of the little, and the likeness of what remains of it is like a *thaghr*—meaning a pool—whose pure water has been drunk and whose turbid water remains."
"1215","[AI-translation] Laythi he said: We used to visit the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, when revelation was sent down upon him, and he would speak to us. He said to us one day: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: We sent down wealth for the establishment of prayer and the giving of zakat. If the son of Adam had a valley, he would desire a second one; and if he had two valleys, he would desire a third. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, then Allah accepts the repentance of whoever repents."
"1216","[AI-translation] From 'A'ishah, raised to the Prophet: Verily Allah loves when one of you does a deed that he perfects it."
"1217","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: Verily Allah loves one who is lenient in selling, lenient in buying, and lenient in settling debts."
"1218","[AI-translation] Rahman ibn Shibl, raised to the Prophet: The merchants are the wicked. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, has Allah not permitted trade? He said: Yes, but they converse and lie, and they swear and commit sin."
"1219","[AI-translation] From 'Abayah ibn Rifa'ah ibn Rafi' ibn Khadij he said: His grandfather, when he died, left a slave-girl, a working camel, a young boy, a cupper, and land. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said concerning the slave-girl: He forbade her earnings. Shu'bah said: Lest she commit fornication. And he said: Whatever the cupper earns, feed it to the working camel. And he said concerning the land: Cultivate it or leave it."
"1220","[AI-translation] From 'Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah he said: He went out with the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, to the prayer place and saw the people buying and selling. He said: O company of merchants! They responded to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, and raised their necks and gazes towards him, and he said: Verily the merchants will be raised on the Day of Resurrection as wicked, except for those who feared Allah, acted righteously, and spoke the truth."
"1221","[AI-translation] Bara' ibn 'Azib he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, came to us at al-Baqi' and said: O company of merchants! When they raised their heads, he said: Verily the merchants will be gathered on the Day of Resurrection as wicked, except those who feared, acted righteously, and spoke the truth."
"1222","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, he said: Dawud, the Prophet, peace be upon him, used not to eat except from the work of his hands."
"1223","[AI-translation] Muttalib: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, entered upon Hamzah and they conversed about the world. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: The world is green and sweet. Whoever takes it by its right, it is blessed for him. And many a one who plunges in the wealth of Allah and the wealth of His Messenger, he has nothing but the Fire on the Day he meets Allah."
"1224","[AI-translation] Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: The world is sweet and green, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has made you successors in it to see how you act. So beware of the world and beware of women, for the first trial of the Children of Israel was concerning women."
"1225","[AI-translation] From 'Uqbah bin 'Amir, marfu'an: Verily, your Lord marvels at a young man who has no youthful folly."
"1226","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, marfu'an: A man used to sell wine in a ship, and he used to mix the wine with water. He had a monkey with him. The monkey took the purse, climbed the mast, and began casting a dinar into the sea and a dinar into the ship, until it halved it."
"1227","[AI-translation] Khayr said: Muslamah bin Mukhlad, who was the governor of Egypt, offered Ruwaifi' bin Thabit to appoint him over the tithes. He replied: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, say: The collector of tolls is in the Fire."
"1228","[AI-translation] From Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, who said: If the Hour is established and in the hand of one of you is a sapling, then if he is able that it should not be established before he plants it, let him plant it."
"1229","[AI-translation] From Mu'awiyah bin Abu Sufyan who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, say: Whatever remains of the world is only a trial and tribulation. And the likeness of the action of one of you is like that of a vessel; if its upper part is pure, its lower part is pure, and if its upper part is foul, its lower part is foul. ( )"
"1230","[AI-translation] From Abu Musa, I think, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: Verily, this dinar and this dirham destroyed those who were before you, and they are your destroyers."
"1231","[AI-translation] From Mu'awiyah, marfu'an: I am only a treasurer, and it is Allah, Mighty and Majestic, Who gives. So whoever I give a gift with a willing heart, then it is that it be blessed for one of you. And whoever I give a gift out of greed and the greed of begging, he is like one who eats and is never satisfied."
"1232","[AI-translation] Rafi' bin Khadij said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, forbade al-muhaqalah and al-muzabanah, and said: Only three types of people plant: a man who has land, so he plants it; a man who is gifted land, so he plants what he was gifted; and a man who rents land for gold or silver."
"1233","[AI-translation] From Yahya bin Ja'dah, who said: A group of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah visited Khabbab and said: Rejoice, Abu 'Abdullah! You will meet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, at the Hawd. He said: What about it or this? And he pointed to the top of his house and the bottom of it. And the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, had said: It is sufficient for one of you to have in the world the like of a rider's provision."
"1234","[AI-translation] From 'Awn bin Abi Juhaifa who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The world will be opened up to you until you furnish your houses as the Ka'bah is furnished."" We said: ""And we are upon our religion today?"" He said: ""And you are upon your religion today."" We said: ""So are we better that day or today?"" He said: ""Rather, you are better today."
"1235","[AI-translation] From Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""Whoever of you has land or palm trees, let him not sell it until he offers it to his partner."
"1236","[AI-translation] From Kurz bin 'Alqamah, raised to the Prophet: ""Any household among the Arabs and non-Arabs whom Allah intends good for, He admits Islam to them, then tribulations will occur as if they are shades."
"1237","[AI-translation] Bariqi, raised to the Prophet: ""Camels are honor for their owners, sheep are a blessing, and good is tied in the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection."
"1238","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""Those with the most are the lowest on the Day of Resurrection, except one who said: 'With wealth, like this and like this' (and his earning is from what is pure)."
"1239","[AI-translation] From Abu Sa'id, who said: An Arab Bedouin passed by with a sheep, and I said: ""Will you sell it for three dirhams?"" He said: ""No, by Allah."" Then he sold it, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and he said: ""He sold his Hereafter for his worldly life."
"1240","On the authority of Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: While a man was in a wilderness, he heard a voice in a cloud saying: ""Water the garden of so-and-so"" — calling him by name. The cloud then moved to a rocky plain and poured out its water. The water flowed into a channel, reached a watercourse, and was absorbed. The man followed the cloud until he came upon a man standing in his garden watering it. He said: ""O servant of Allah, what is your name?"" He replied: ""Why do you ask?"" He said: ""I heard a voice in this cloud, whose water this is, saying: 'Water the garden of so-and-so' — by your name. So what do you do with it when you harvest it?"" He said: ""Since you have said that, I divide it into three thirds: I allocate one third for myself and my family, I reinvest one third back into it, and I give one third to the poor, the needy, and the wayfarer."""
"1241","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The trustworthy, truthful Muslim merchant is with (the Prophets, the truthful, and) the martyrs on the Day of Resurrection."
"1242","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, who said: ""Three are all unlawful consumption: the earnings of a cupper, the dowry of a prostitute, and the price of a dog, except a hunting dog."
"1243","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin 'Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""The price of wine is forbidden, and the dowry of a prostitute is forbidden, and the price of a dog is forbidden, and the Kubah is forbidden. And if the owner of a dog comes to you seeking its price, fill his hands with dust. Wine, gambling, and every intoxicant are forbidden."
"1244","[AI-translation] From Rafi' bin Khadij that the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""The price of a dog is evil, the dowry of a prostitute is evil, and the earnings of a cupper are evil."
"1245","Ibn Abbas said: A man came to Umar asking him, so he kept looking at his head once and at his feet another time, to see if he perceived any sign of hardship. Then Umar said to him: ""How much wealth do you have?"" He said: ""Forty camels."" Ibn Abbas said: ""Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth: 'If the son of Adam had two valleys of gold, he would desire a third, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to him who repents.'"" Umar said: ""What is this?"" I said: ""This is how Ubayy recited it to me."" He said: ""Then let us go to him."" So he came to Ubayy and said: ""What does this man say?"" Ubayy said: ""This is how the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) recited it to me."""
"1246","[AI-translation] Hasan, the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The best provision is sufficiency."
"1247","[AI-translation] Rahib, narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him): A dirham of usury that a man consumes knowingly is more severe in the sight of Allah than thirty-six acts of fornication."
"1248","[AI-translation] From Hakim bin Abi Yazid, from his father, from someone who heard the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) say: Leave the people be, let some of them strike others; but if a man seeks sincere advice from his brother, let him advise him sincerely."
"1249","[AI-translation] From Umm Ayman: She sifted flour and made a loaf of bread for the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family). He asked: What is this? She said: It is food we make in our land, and I wanted to make a loaf for you from it. He said: Return it to it, then knead it."
"1250","[AI-translation] Bara' bin 'Azib, narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him): Usury has seventy-two doors, the least of which is like a man having relations with his mother, and the most usurious of usury is a man transgressing against the honor of his brother."
"1251","[AI-translation] From 'Umar bin Sa'd he said: I had a need with Abu Sa'd. He said: Abu Hayyan narrated to us from Mujammi', he said: 'Umar bin Sa'd had a need with his father. He preceded his request with words from what people say to establish rapport, which he had not heard before. When he finished, he said: O my son! Have you finished your speech? He said: Yes. He said: You were never further from having your need met, nor was I ever less desirous of you than I have been since I heard these words of yours. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: There will be a people who eat with their tongues as a cow eats from the ground."
"1252","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him): The old man grows old and his body weakens, but his heart remains young upon the love of two things: long life and the love of wealth."
"1253","[AI-translation] From 'Abdullah bin 'Amr he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: The righteousness of the early part of this nation is through asceticism and certainty, and its latter part will perish through stinginess and hope."
"1254","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him): Iblis said: For all Your creation You have clarified their provision, so in what is my provision? He said: In that upon which My name is not mentioned."
"1255","[AI-translation] 'As, narrated from the Prophet (peace be upon him): He has truly succeeded who submits (to Islam), is provided with sufficiency, and whom Allah has made content with what He has given him."
"1256","[AI-translation] Anas said: There were two brothers during the time of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family. One of them used to come to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, and in a narration: he used to attend the discourse and gathering of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family. And the other used to work. So the worker complained about his brother to the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family (and he said: O Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him! (This) is my brother, he does not help me with anything). He, peace be upon him, said: Perhaps you are provided for through him."
"1257","[AI-translation] An-Nu'man said: He, peace be upon him and his family, could not find enough al-daql to fill his stomach while he was hungry. ( )"
"1258","[AI-translation] Ibn Abbas said: He, peace be upon him and his family, used to spend consecutive nights with an empty stomach, and his family had no supper, and most of their bread was barley."
"1259","[AI-translation] Anas ibn Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, said: He, peace be upon him and his family, used to be invited to barley bread and rancid fat, and he would accept."
"1260","[AI-translation] Ibn Umar said: A man belched in the presence of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, so he said: ""Restrain your belching from us, for the most satiated of them in this world will be the hungriest of them on the Day of Resurrection."
"1261","[AI-translation] Bakhtari said: I heard a hadith from a man and it impressed me, so I said: ""Write it down for me."" He brought it written on a shoulder-blade: Al-Abbas and Ali entered upon Umar, and with him were Talha, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman, and Sa'd, and the two were disputing. Umar said to Talha, al-Zubayr, Abd al-Rahman, and Sa'd: ""Did you not know that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: 'All the wealth of the Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, is charity except what he feeds his family and clothes them. We are not inherited from.' They said: ""Yes."" He said: ""So the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, used to spend from his wealth on his family and give the rest in charity. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, passed away, and Abu Bakr took charge of it for two years, and he used to do what the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, used to do. Then he mentioned something from the hadith of Malik ibn Aws."
"1262","[AI-translation] Every good deed you do to a rich or poor person is charity. It was narrated from the hadith of Ibn Mas'ud and Jabir."
"1263","[AI-translation] Abdullah ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, took hold of my shoulder and said: ""Be in this world as if you are a stranger or a wayfarer."
"1264","[AI-translation] Abdullah ibn Amr said: The Prophet, peace be upon him and his family, said to a man: ""How are you this morning, O so-and-so?"" He said: ""I praise Allah to you, O Messenger of Allah!"" The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: ""This is what I wanted from you."" ( )"
"1265","[AI-translation] Ismail ibn Abdullah said: Anas ibn Malik came to al-Walid ibn Abd al-Malik, and al-Walid said to him: ""What did you hear the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, mention regarding the Hour?"" He narrated that the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, said: ""I am not of this world, nor is it of me. I was sent, and the Hour and I race."
"1266","[AI-translation] From Fudalah bin 'Ubayd who said: Whenever the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, led the people in prayer, men would fall from their standing positions due to the hunger they suffered, and they were among the People of the Suffah, to the point that the Bedouins would say: ""These people are mad."" When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, finished the prayer, he would turn to them and say: ""If you knew what you have with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, you would love to increase in need and poverty."
"1267","Umm Salamah said: ""Abu Bakr went out on a trading journey to Busra during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Abu Bakr's stinginess regarding his share of setting out for trade did not prevent him from accompanying the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and that was due to their admiration for the earnings of trade and their love for trade. And the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prevent Abu Bakr from setting out in his trade due to his love for his companionship and his good opinion of Abu Bakr, for he was pleased with his companionship, due to the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ approval of trade — and in another narration: his love for trade — and his admiration for it."""
"1268","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: If the son of Adam had two valleys of wealth (in a narration: of gold), he would seek a third (valley). Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah accepts the repentance of whoever repents. It was narrated from the Prophet, peace be upon him, by a group of his Companions, among them: Anas, Ibn 'Abbas, Ibn al-Zubayr, and Abu Musa, may Allah be pleased with them."
"1269","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, raised to the Prophet: If I had gold equal to Mount Uhud, it would please me that no three nights pass by me while I have anything of it, except something I reserve for a debt."
"1270","[AI-translation] He said, peace be upon him: If the world were equal in the sight of Allah to the wing of a mosquito, He would not give a disbeliever a drink of water from it. It was narrated in the hadith of Sahl bin Sa'd, Abu Hurayrah, 'Abdullah bin 'Amr, 'Abdullah bin 'Abbas, and a group of the Companions, may Allah be pleased with them, and Al-Hasan and 'Amr bin Murrah as a mursal narration."
"1271","[AI-translation] From Sahl bin Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, said: If the world were equal in the sight of Allah to the wing of a mosquito, He would not give a disbeliever a drink of water from it."
"1272","[AI-translation] Aslami who said: He came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, asking him for help regarding the dowry of a woman. He said: ""How much did you give her as a dowry?"" He said: ""Two hundred dirhams."" He said, peace be upon him: ""Even if you were scooping from Batihan, you would not have exceeded this."
"1273","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Abbas, raised to the Prophet: Let one of you be independent of the people, even if with a stick of siwak."
"1274","[AI-translation] Aslami, raised to the Prophet: Let it suffice one of you from this world to have a servant and a mount."
"1275","[AI-translation] Darda' who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him and his family, was asked about the wealth of the ruler? He said: Whatever comes to you from the wealth of the ruler without asking or looking forward to it, then eat it and possess it."
"1276","[AI-translation] From Abu Dharr, may Allah be pleased with him, raised to the Prophet: I would not love that Mount Uhud were mine in gold, such that on the third night a dinar of it is with me, except a dinar I reserve for a debt, unless I distribute it among the servants of Allah like this - and he scattered it in front of him - and like this to his right, and like this to his left."
"1277","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), raised: I do not fear poverty upon you, but I fear upon you the competition for abundance, and I do not fear error upon you, but I fear deliberate action upon you."
"1278","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said during his illness in which he died: ""O Aishah! What has the gold done?"" She said: I said, ""It is with me."" He said: ""Bring it to me."" So I brought it, and it was between nine or five. He placed it in his hand, then gestured with it, and Yazid gestured with his hand: ""What would Muhammad think of Allah if he were to meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and this was with him? Spend it."
"1279","Abū Umāmah ibn Sahl said: I and ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr entered one day upon ʿĀʾishah, and she said: ""If you had seen the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a day during an illness he suffered."" She said: ""He had with me six dinars."" Mūsā said: ""Or seven."" She said: ""So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded me to distribute them."" She said: ""But the pain of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ preoccupied me until Allah cured him."" She said: ""Then he asked me about them. He said: 'What did the six do?' He said: 'Or the seven?' I said: 'No, by Allah, your pain preoccupied me.'"" She said: ""So he called for them, then arranged them in his palm, and said: 'What does the Messenger of Allah think he would say if he met Allah, Mighty and Majestic, while these are with him?' Meaning six dinars or seven."""
"1280","[AI-translation] Narrated Anas: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: There is no Muslim who plants a plant or sows a crop, and a bird, human, or beast eats from it, except that it is a charity for him."
"1281","[AI-translation] Narrated Jabir, raised: There is no Muslim who plants a plant except that what is eaten from it is a charity for him, and what is stolen from it is a charity for him, and what the wild beast eats from it is a charity for him, and what the birds eat is a charity for him, and no one diminishes it except that it is a charity for him, until the Day of Resurrection."
"1282","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), raised: It does not please me to have [gold equal to] Uhud of gold, when the third [day] comes upon me and I have a dinar of it, except a dinar I set aside for a debt upon me."
"1283","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Amr, raised: The likeness of the one who takes back what he gifted is like that of a dog which vomits and then eats its vomit. If the giver takes it back, he should be stopped, he should be informed of what he took back, then what he gifted should be given to him."
"1284","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) said: Whoever hoards goods intending to raise their prices against the Muslims, he is a wrongdoer."
"1285","[AI-translation] Narrated Ubaidullah bin Abdullah bin Utbah: Maimunah, the wife of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family), took a debt. It was said to her: ""O Mother of the Believers! You take a debt while you do not have the means to pay it?"" She said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: Whoever takes a debt intending to repay it, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will help him."
"1286","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Masud, raised: Whoever is afflicted with poverty and brings it upon the people, his poverty will not be relieved. And whoever brings it upon Allah, He will soon bring him richness, either by a swift death or a swift richness."
"1287","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Shuraih: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Whoever cancels a sale for his brother, Allah will cancel his slip on the Day of Resurrection."
"1288","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah, traced back to the Prophet: Whoever makes two sales in one sale, then he has the lesser of the two, or it is Riba."
"1289","[AI-translation] Yaman who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Whoever sells a house and does not put its price into something like it, there is no blessing for him in it."
"1290","[AI-translation] Sakan who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) say: Whoever leaves behind two dinars has left behind two Kayyahs."
"1291","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Whoever begs while he has what suffices him, his begging will come on the Day of Resurrection as scratches, gouges, or lacerations on his face. It was said: O Messenger of Allah! And what suffices him? He said: Fifty dirhams or its value in gold."
"1292","[AI-translation] Narrated Abdullah bin Mas'ud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: Whoever deceives us is not from us, and deceit and deception are in the Fire."
"1293","[AI-translation] Khattab were discussing charity one day. Umar said: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) when he mentioned the misappropriation of charity, that whoever misappropriates from it – meaning from charity – a camel or a sheep, he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection carrying it...? Abdullah bin Unais said: Yes."
"1294","[AI-translation] Narrated Aishah that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) say: Whoever is in debt and intends to repay it, he will have help from Allah, and Allah will provide for him a means of provision."
"1295","[AI-translation] Narrated Ibn Abbas from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) who said: Whoever has land and wants to sell it, let him offer it to his neighbor."
"1296","[AI-translation] The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: The Muslims are bound by their conditions. This was narrated from a group of the Companions of the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) from the hadith of Abu Hurairah, Aishah, Anas bin Malik, Amr bin Awf, Rafi bin Khadij, and Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"1297","[AI-translation] Narrated Abu Hurairah who said: A man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) asking him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him and his family) borrowed half a Wasq for him and gave it to him. The man came to demand repayment, so he gave him a Wasq and said: Half is for you as repayment, and half is for you as a gift from me."
"1298","[AI-translation] From Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, forbid withholding the surplus water of a well, meaning the excess water."
"1299","[AI-translation] Ansari, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, forbade the price of a dog and a cat."
"1300","[AI-translation] meaning Al-Husayn - raised to the Prophet: He forbade harvesting at night and reaping at night. Jafar bin Muhammad said: I think it was because of the poor."
"1301","[AI-translation] From Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, forbid the earnings of a flutist."
"1302","[AI-translation] From Anas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, saying: By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the family of Muhammad did not have a sa' of grain nor a sa' of dates in the morning."
"1303","[AI-translation] From Aishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: A woman from the Ansar entered upon me and saw the bed of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him and his family, which was a folded blanket. She left and sent to him a bed stuffed with wool. The Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, entered upon me and said: ""What is this?"" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! So-and-so Al-Ansariyyah entered upon me and saw your bed, then she left and sent this."" He said: ""Return it."" I did not return it, and it pleased me that it be in my house, until he said that three times. Then he said: ""By Allah, O Aishah! If I wished, Allah would make flow with me mountains of gold and silver."
"1304","[AI-translation] From Jabir, raised to the Prophet: There is no harm in one animal for two, hand to hand."
"1305","[AI-translation] From Khawwat bin Jubayr, he said: A man died and left a will with me. Among what he bequeathed was his umm walad and a free woman. An argument occurred between the umm walad and the wife. The wife said to her: ""O base one! Tomorrow your ear will be seized and you will be sold in the market!"" I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him, and he said: ""An umm walad is not to be sold."
"1306","[AI-translation] From Abu Umamah from the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him: Do not sell singing slave-girls, nor buy them, nor teach them, and there is no good in trade involving them, and their price is unlawful. And regarding something like this, this verse was revealed: ""And of the people is he who buys the amusement of speech to mislead from the way of Allah without knowledge"" (Luqman: 6) to the end of the verse."
"1307","[AI-translation] From Ibn Masud, raised to the Prophet: Do not acquire estates, lest you desire the worldly life."
"1308","[AI-translation] From 'Uqbah bin 'Amir, raised to the Prophet: Do not frighten yourselves after attaining security. They asked: And what is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Debt."
"1309","[AI-translation] Bahili who said: He saw a plowshare and something from a farming tool, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, say: This does not enter the house of a people except that Allah enters humiliation into it."
"1310","On the authority of Abu Hurayrah: A man insulted Abu Bakr while the Prophet (peace be upon him) was sitting. The Prophet (peace be upon him) began to wonder and smile. When the man persisted, Abu Bakr responded to some of his words. The Prophet (peace be upon him) became angry and stood up. Abu Bakr followed him and said: ""O Messenger of Allah! He was insulting me while you were sitting. When I responded to some of his words, you became angry and stood up."" He said: ""There was an angel with you responding on your behalf. When you responded to some of his words, the devil descended, and I could not sit with the devil."" Then he said: ""O Abu Bakr! Three things, all of them are true: No servant is wronged by an injustice and overlooks it for the sake of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, except that Allah strengthens his victory thereby. And no man opens a door of giving seeking to maintain ties of kinship except that Allah increases him in abundance thereby. And no man opens a door of asking seeking abundance except that Allah increases him in scarcity thereby."""
"1311","[AI-translation] From Ibn 'Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him and his family, sent Sa'd bin 'Ubadah as a collector of Zakah. He said: ""O Sa'd! Fear lest you come on the Day of Resurrection carrying a camel that is grumbling."" He said: ""I will not take it, excuse me."" So he excused him."
